WEBVTT


00:00:01.691 --> 00:00:03.955
It's not the amount of
federal money allocated to it


00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:06.985
so much as how research
priorities are defined.


00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:08.792
- We need new drugs
to keep people alive,


00:00:08.831 --> 00:00:10.958
but the NIH
is only testing old drugs,


00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.228
drugs that we already have.


00:00:12.268 --> 00:00:13.633
- Can you tell us
what you're doing?


00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:15.136
- Hi, I'm Jim Jenson,


00:00:15.171 --> 00:00:16.968
and I'm in
a clinical trial here.


00:00:17.006 --> 00:00:18.098
And right now,


00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.131
I'm observing
and participating in


00:00:20.176 --> 00:00:21.643
the ACT UP demonstration.


00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:23.269
- Why?
Why do you support this action?


00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:26.145
- Because we need
far more AIDS research.


00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:27.308
And we're just beginning.


00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.715
- What trial are you in?


00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:32.312
- I'm in interleukin-2 AZT
combination study.


00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:33.982
- Are there any women
in your trial?


00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:35.490
- No, there aren't any women
at all.


00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:36.651
- People of color?


00:00:36.692 --> 00:00:38.319
- Uh, no, there are not.


00:00:38.361 --> 00:00:39.555
- Why do you think that is?


00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.495
Just the beginning
of the problem.


00:00:42.532 --> 00:00:43.863
Murder, murder!


00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.026
- There are three major things


00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.500
that control NIH research:


00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:49.505
stupidity, incompetence,
and greed.


00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:51.336
Those are the three major
driving forces


00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:52.500
behind what's going on here


00:00:52.542 --> 00:00:54.134
and why there are
no treatments out there


00:00:54.176 --> 00:00:55.609
for people
living with this disease.


00:00:56.879 --> 00:00:58.176
In that building
down that way,


00:00:58.214 --> 00:01:00.842
Dr. Anthony Fauci is deciding
the research priorities


00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:01.941
for the National Institutes


00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:04.077
of Allergy
and Infectious Diseases.


00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.417
We're down here
'cause we think


00:01:05.454 --> 00:01:07.046
we should be deciding
the research priorities,


00:01:07.089 --> 00:01:08.818
because these are the people
who know what's going on


00:01:08.858 --> 00:01:10.519
'cause they're dealing with it
every day.


00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:22.734
The whole world
is watching!


00:01:22.772 --> 00:01:24.535
The whole world is watching!


00:01:24.574 --> 00:01:26.371
The whole world
is watching!


00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:28.036
The whole world is watching!


00:01:28.077 --> 00:01:29.840
The whole world
is watching!


00:01:29.879 --> 00:01:31.870
The whole world is watching!


00:01:31.914 --> 00:01:34.109
The whole world
is watching!


00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.708
The whole world is watching!


00:01:35.751 --> 00:01:37.548
The whole world
is watching!


00:02:08.451 --> 00:02:10.578
- If anything,
the mood after the NIH


00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.417
was even bleaker
than the mood before,


00:02:12.455 --> 00:02:13.786
because we had no indication


00:02:13.823 --> 00:02:17.418
that they were gonna change
or respond to our demands,


00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.758
and we had in fact had a meeting
with them in Bethesda


00:02:19.795 --> 00:02:20.921
after the NIH action


00:02:20.963 --> 00:02:22.931
that indicated
that there was total resistance


00:02:22.965 --> 00:02:24.762
to putting people
from the community


00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.097
on the research committees,


00:02:26.135 --> 00:02:28.763
to letting the ACT UP observers
attend the meetings,


00:02:28.804 --> 00:02:29.930
and to open up the meetings


00:02:29.972 --> 00:02:31.439
so that
they weren't secret anymore.


00:02:31.474 --> 00:02:33.271
Why should science
be shrouded in secrecy?


00:02:33.309 --> 00:02:36.278
It's supposed to be based on
a free exchange of ideas.


00:02:36.312 --> 00:02:40.146
And so it was very important
to stage in San Francisco--


00:02:40.182 --> 00:02:42.616
before, again, the global
community of scientists


00:02:42.652 --> 00:02:44.119
and people working on AIDS--


00:02:44.153 --> 00:02:45.950
why we had been at the NIH,


00:02:45.988 --> 00:02:48.456
why the U.S. system
wasn't working out,


00:02:48.491 --> 00:02:50.459
and to reach the people
directly


00:02:50.493 --> 00:02:54.122
that we had reached symbolically
through the NIH action.


00:03:08.344 --> 00:03:10.642
- About 100 protesters
have already been arrested


00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.204
at the International
AIDS Conference


00:03:12.248 --> 00:03:14.546
that began today
in San Francisco.


00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:16.380
Hundreds more
are angrily protesting


00:03:16.419 --> 00:03:17.613
a government policy


00:03:17.653 --> 00:03:21.555
they say neglects research
and ostracizes victims.


00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.081
- Why don't you do
an informational slide first?


00:03:24.126 --> 00:03:26.321
"United States
has the most discriminatory


00:03:26.362 --> 00:03:28.489
immigration policies
regarding HIV."


00:03:28.531 --> 00:03:33.662
- I could say, you know,
as a way to bridge the, uh--


00:03:33.703 --> 00:03:36.831
the rift between the scientific
community--all of you--


00:03:36.872 --> 00:03:40.501
and the activists, we'd like you
to join in some activism.


00:03:40.543 --> 00:03:42.511
And I've always been
painfully aware


00:03:42.545 --> 00:03:45.844
that in order for me
to beat this virus and live,


00:03:45.881 --> 00:03:48.042
I will need a great deal of help
from all of you.


00:03:50.052 --> 00:03:51.519
Can we all,


00:03:51.554 --> 00:03:52.680
before it's too late,


00:03:52.722 --> 00:03:55.350
begin to understand
each other?


00:03:55.391 --> 00:04:00.693
Will we realize that
we share similar motivations?


00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.288
During the upcoming days,


00:04:02.331 --> 00:04:04.526
ACT UP New York
will be handing out


00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.364
our AIDS Treatment Agenda,


00:04:06.402 --> 00:04:08.870
which includes a list
of 99 drugs


00:04:08.904 --> 00:04:10.531
that we believe
could be ready


00:04:10.573 --> 00:04:14.065
for small Phase I studies
this year or next.


00:04:15.745 --> 00:04:18.373
However, from your side,


00:04:18.414 --> 00:04:22.214
we're being constantly told
to butt out.


00:04:22.251 --> 00:04:26.051
On my side, the level
of anger and frustration


00:04:26.088 --> 00:04:27.715
is reaching such a point


00:04:27.757 --> 00:04:32.057
that attitudes claiming that
all of you are uncaring


00:04:32.094 --> 00:04:36.224
and in it for greed
are now widespread.


00:04:36.265 --> 00:04:38.893
While at times
we may offend you,


00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:41.562
remember as well that
like you,


00:04:41.604 --> 00:04:44.903
ACT UP has succeeded
in prolonging the lives


00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.909
of thousands of people
living with HIV disease.


00:04:52.615 --> 00:04:55.584
I would like to be joined
in front of the stage


00:04:55.618 --> 00:04:57.745
by my fellow AIDS activists.


00:04:57.787 --> 00:04:59.015
Would you all come up?


00:05:00.222 --> 00:05:04.921
At this moment,
there are others just like us


00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.928
who are trying
to get into this conference


00:05:06.962 --> 00:05:09.089
but are being barred
by the billy clubs


00:05:09.131 --> 00:05:11.258
of San Francisco police.


00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.268
And there are
still others like us


00:05:13.302 --> 00:05:14.929
who are trying
to get through customs


00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.767
at the San Francisco airport


00:05:16.806 --> 00:05:20.469
but are being detained instead
because they are gay.


00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:23.774
There's a man that could have
prevented these absurdities.


00:05:23.813 --> 00:05:25.110
This man has said that


00:05:25.147 --> 00:05:28.275
he would like to see
a kinder, gentler nation.


00:05:28.317 --> 00:05:30.615
If you believe
that the immigration policy


00:05:30.653 --> 00:05:32.780
barring people
living with HIV disease


00:05:32.822 --> 00:05:35.620
from entering this country
is useless as a health policy


00:05:35.658 --> 00:05:37.455
and discriminatory as well,


00:05:37.493 --> 00:05:42.294
please stand now
and remain standing.


00:05:44.166 --> 00:05:47.624
Join us in vocalizing
our collective anger.


00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:49.968
Join us
in a chant against the man


00:05:50.005 --> 00:05:51.802
who could bring down
the INS barriers.


00:05:51.841 --> 00:05:54.469
Join us
in a chant against the man


00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:55.602
who has decided to show


00:05:55.644 --> 00:05:57.305
his commitment
to fighting AIDS


00:05:57.346 --> 00:05:59.314
by refusing to be here today.


00:05:59.348 --> 00:06:02.317
Instead,
he is, at this very moment,


00:06:02.351 --> 00:06:05.218
in North Carolina,
attending a fund-raiser


00:06:05.254 --> 00:06:08.485
for the homophobic author
of the INS barriers,


00:06:08.524 --> 00:06:10.822
that pig in the senate
known as Jesse Helms.


00:06:12.194 --> 00:06:14.128
Join us in this chant:


00:06:14.163 --> 00:06:15.994
300,000 dead from AIDS.


00:06:16.031 --> 00:06:17.999
Where is George?


00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:20.501
300,000 dead from AIDS.


00:06:20.536 --> 00:06:22.163
Where is George?


00:06:22.204 --> 00:06:24.365
300,000 dead from AIDS.


00:06:24.406 --> 00:06:26.306
Where is George?


00:06:26.342 --> 00:06:28.674
300,000 dead from AIDS.


00:06:28.711 --> 00:06:30.804
Where is George?


00:06:30.846 --> 00:06:33.007
- You can all
now consider yourselves


00:06:33.048 --> 00:06:34.675
members of ACT UP.


00:06:42.892 --> 00:06:45.019
- One of the things
that happened in San Francisco


00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:48.860
was that we found out we had won
some of our NIH demands.


00:06:48.898 --> 00:06:51.025
Fauci came up to me and said,
"We had a meeting.


00:06:51.066 --> 00:06:52.465
"We decided that
we're gonna put you guys


00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:53.934
"on all the committees,


00:06:53.969 --> 00:06:55.664
"and we're gonna let your
observers go to the meetings,


00:06:55.704 --> 00:06:57.001
and the meetings
won't be secret anymore."


00:06:57.039 --> 00:07:00.497
- Never again


00:07:00.542 --> 00:07:03.705
could any of this be done


00:07:03.746 --> 00:07:07.045
without taking people with AIDS
and their advocates


00:07:07.082 --> 00:07:08.709
into consideration.


00:07:08.751 --> 00:07:14.587
This would be public business
from now on.


00:07:14.623 --> 00:07:16.887
- You know, we should all
be going through the bushes


00:07:16.926 --> 00:07:20.054
like this,
like, sticking our heads up.


00:07:20.095 --> 00:07:21.858
It was beginning to feel
a little different


00:07:21.897 --> 00:07:23.762
because we'd spent all the time
up until then


00:07:23.799 --> 00:07:25.061
being on the outside,


00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.227
sort of beating on the doors
and trying to get in,


00:07:27.269 --> 00:07:29.737
and now they actually wanted
to hear what we had to say.


00:07:46.789 --> 00:07:48.757
- We brought them in
at Merck.


00:07:48.791 --> 00:07:51.419
We made--we made
a very specific effort


00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.087
to bring
those individuals in


00:07:53.128 --> 00:07:55.688
so that they would see
what it is that we were doing--


00:07:55.731 --> 00:07:57.358
or trying to do--
from the very beginning.


00:07:57.399 --> 00:07:59.924
- This was really fantastic
stuff


00:07:59.969 --> 00:08:03.097
because we were sitting down
with them, and--


00:08:03.138 --> 00:08:05.436
sometimes from
the very earliest stages


00:08:05.474 --> 00:08:06.771
of the development
of a drug--


00:08:06.809 --> 00:08:09.277
and helping them plot out
their strategy


00:08:09.311 --> 00:08:11.643
toward designing
clinical trials.


00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.114
- The chemists who had worked
on the project,


00:08:14.149 --> 00:08:16.049
a bunch--
a couple chemists said,


00:08:16.085 --> 00:08:18.883
"Let's look at all
the aspartic protease inhibitors


00:08:18.921 --> 00:08:20.286
that we have on the shelf."


00:08:20.322 --> 00:08:21.789
And they tested 'em,


00:08:21.824 --> 00:08:24.657
and they found a few molecules
that actually worked.


00:08:24.693 --> 00:08:27.127
The challenge was,
is now you had these molecules


00:08:27.162 --> 00:08:30.461
that were really good inhibitors
in your assay,


00:08:30.499 --> 00:08:32.296
which is just in a test tube.


00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:33.961
When you put it into animals,


00:08:34.003 --> 00:08:35.129
they just would never work,


00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.468
or they would never get absorbed
by your system.


00:08:37.506 --> 00:08:39.064
- And I remember
being very disappointed


00:08:39.108 --> 00:08:40.769
'cause I had to share
this information


00:08:40.809 --> 00:08:43.471
with sort of my own
personal view, which was,


00:08:43.512 --> 00:08:44.979
this is gonna be
a lot more difficult than,


00:08:45.014 --> 00:08:46.641
you know, we thought
it was gonna be originally


00:08:46.682 --> 00:08:48.309
and in fact
may not be possible.


00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:50.318
And Bill Bahlman said,
"Take a break,


00:08:50.352 --> 00:08:52.479
pick yourself up,
and go back at it."


00:08:52.521 --> 00:08:55.820
If he and his colleagues
and his friends around the table


00:08:55.858 --> 00:08:57.485
can take that attitude
and do that,


00:08:57.526 --> 00:08:58.857
I remember saying to myself,


00:08:58.894 --> 00:09:01.488
"Emilio, you've got no right
to say to yourself,


00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:03.896
'I don't know if I can do this,'
all right?"


00:09:03.932 --> 00:09:06.662
And so off we went.


00:09:06.702 --> 00:09:08.829
And we kept going at it.


00:09:08.871 --> 00:09:12.363
- We're spending $4 billion
a year on AIDS research.


00:09:12.408 --> 00:09:14.672
When you consider that
on a per capita basis for--


00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:17.008
compared to heart disease
or cancer,


00:09:17.046 --> 00:09:18.343
it's an awful lot.


00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.678
- Almost nothing
stops George Bush


00:09:20.716 --> 00:09:21.842
from a round of golf.


00:09:21.884 --> 00:09:23.351
He's played nearly every day-


00:09:23.385 --> 00:09:24.852
and sometimes twice a day-


00:09:24.887 --> 00:09:26.354
during his August vacation.


00:09:29.658 --> 00:09:30.852
- ♪ I'll be glad ♪


00:09:30.893 --> 00:09:32.724
♪ When you're dead,
you rascal, you ♪


00:09:32.761 --> 00:09:33.728
- ♪ Rascal, you ♪


00:09:33.762 --> 00:09:35.024
- ♪ I'll be laughin' ♪


00:09:35.064 --> 00:09:36.964
♪ When you're in your grave,
you dog ♪


00:09:36.999 --> 00:09:38.261
- ♪ Dirty dog ♪


00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.029
- ♪ When you're dead
and in your grave ♪


00:09:40.069 --> 00:09:42.037
♪ No more ravioli
will you crave ♪


00:09:42.071 --> 00:09:44.198
- If the message is research,


00:09:44.239 --> 00:09:46.036
I would say
please talk to Dr. Fauci


00:09:46.075 --> 00:09:48.373
and others at the National
Institute of Health,


00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.105
who will tell you that


00:09:50.145 --> 00:09:53.546
we're doing pretty well
in funding of research.


00:09:53.582 --> 00:09:54.674
- ♪ Dirty dog ♪


00:09:54.716 --> 00:09:56.946
- ♪ I invite you
to my house for a meal ♪


00:09:56.985 --> 00:09:59.510
♪ All my meatballs
you tried to steal ♪


00:09:59.555 --> 00:10:00.886
♪ Mm ♪


00:10:00.923 --> 00:10:03.187
♪ You're a devil, yeah ♪


00:10:03.225 --> 00:10:05.284
- Act up!
Fight back!


00:10:05.327 --> 00:10:06.385
Fight AIDS!


00:10:17.806 --> 00:10:20.036
- We've got to factor in


00:10:20.075 --> 00:10:25.604
the sensitivity
of those of us


00:10:25.647 --> 00:10:31.085
who feel that there's
a spiritual and moral aspect


00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:34.920
to this playing
to the homosexual,


00:10:34.957 --> 00:10:36.117
lesbian crowd.


00:10:37.359 --> 00:10:40.487
It makes it different
from anything else.


00:10:40.529 --> 00:10:41.826
- Oh, sh--


00:10:41.864 --> 00:10:44.594
- I wish they'd shut
their mouths and go to work


00:10:44.633 --> 00:10:46.931
and keep their private matters
to themselves


00:10:46.969 --> 00:10:49.563
and get their mentality
out of their crotches.


00:10:49.605 --> 00:10:51.505
- I'm here today because
Jesse Helms is the devil.


00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.440
Jesse Helms
has worked for years


00:10:53.475 --> 00:10:55.102
to do as much
as he possibly can


00:10:55.144 --> 00:10:57.044
to ensure the continuance
of the AIDS epidemic.


00:10:57.079 --> 00:10:58.944
- The disease is spreading
because of him,


00:10:58.981 --> 00:11:01.006
and people are dying
because of him.


00:11:01.049 --> 00:11:02.448
- This is an educational effort.


00:11:02.484 --> 00:11:04.748
It's not a violation
of people's property rights.


00:11:04.786 --> 00:11:07.346
We've been very careful that
absolutely no damage is done,


00:11:07.389 --> 00:11:08.788
and if any damage is done,


00:11:08.824 --> 00:11:11.122
whatever it is,
we'll be happy to pay for it.


00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.926
We have the money with us
to pay for it.


00:11:14.963 --> 00:11:16.396
- You guys don't want to tangle
with these people


00:11:16.431 --> 00:11:17.420
'cause you don't want
to get AIDS.


00:11:17.466 --> 00:11:19.491
I know, but what's next?


00:11:19.535 --> 00:11:21.162
Come on, get out.


00:11:21.203 --> 00:11:23.137
- If they would
keep their mouths shut


00:11:23.172 --> 00:11:24.639
and go about their business


00:11:24.673 --> 00:11:27.301
with whatever
their sexual orientation is,


00:11:27.342 --> 00:11:28.536
nobody would ever say a word,


00:11:28.577 --> 00:11:30.135
and we wouldn't know anything
about it.


00:11:30.179 --> 00:11:31.806
But, no,
they march in the streets,


00:11:31.847 --> 00:11:35.647
and they defy you to say
anything about it.


00:11:35.684 --> 00:11:37.584
Well, they don't like me,
and I don't like them.


00:11:37.619 --> 00:11:38.984
- Back off the property.


00:11:39.021 --> 00:11:41.888
- Bunch of 'em climbed up
on my house in Arlington


00:11:41.924 --> 00:11:46.793
and hoisted about
a 35-foot canvas, uh, condom,


00:11:46.828 --> 00:11:48.989
one day,
in protest of me.


00:11:50.999 --> 00:11:52.091
- Fight AIDS!
Fight AIDS!


00:11:52.134 --> 00:11:54.534
Fight AIDS!
Fight!


00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:55.764
- ♪ I'll be glad ♪


00:11:55.804 --> 00:12:00.104
♪ When you're dead,
you rascal, you ♪


00:12:01.243 --> 00:12:02.710
- Sir, when we started
this colloquy,


00:12:02.744 --> 00:12:04.234
I thought
I was on your side,


00:12:04.279 --> 00:12:06.747
particularly
on the First Amendment.


00:12:06.782 --> 00:12:08.044
And under
the First Amendment,


00:12:08.083 --> 00:12:09.641
people don't have to
shut their mouths.


00:12:09.685 --> 00:12:12.017
They have a right to speak.


00:12:12.054 --> 00:12:15.490
- Well, uh...they can speak,


00:12:15.524 --> 00:12:17.651
uh, just so long as, uh,


00:12:17.693 --> 00:12:19.320
they don't offend
anybody else,


00:12:19.361 --> 00:12:21.261
uh, I suppose.


00:12:26.735 --> 00:12:29.033
- Make sure your second coming


00:12:29.071 --> 00:12:30.902
is a safe one.


00:12:33.742 --> 00:12:36.040
Use condoms.


00:12:36.078 --> 00:12:37.375
Are you shooting?


00:12:37.412 --> 00:12:38.709
- Yeah.


00:12:38.747 --> 00:12:42.808
I just turned it on.


00:12:42.851 --> 00:12:44.409
Okay, rolling.


00:12:49.424 --> 00:12:50.550
Tell him we're rolling.


00:12:50.592 --> 00:12:51.718
- The machine is rolling.


00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.251
You can start talking now,
honey.


00:12:54.296 --> 00:12:57.390
- Oh, I didn't know
she meant now.


00:12:57.432 --> 00:13:00.230
What I was gonna say was,
I just love--


00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:03.761
I love so much
to go up to the tenth floor


00:13:03.805 --> 00:13:08.242
because no one
ever had explained to me


00:13:08.277 --> 00:13:14.079
that there was going to be light
again in the world


00:13:14.116 --> 00:13:18.883
and that the whole world
wasn't going to be dark.


00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:24.256
Some great challenges face us
as young people.


00:13:24.293 --> 00:13:27.262
We're in our 20s, and--


00:13:27.296 --> 00:13:29.093
and this is the challenge


00:13:29.131 --> 00:13:31.759
that's been placed
in front of me.


00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.325
And, who knows,
little camera.


00:13:34.369 --> 00:13:37.600
Lots of other blind, deaf men


00:13:37.639 --> 00:13:39.971
have lived happy lives.


00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:46.144
There are--
there are many years to come.


00:13:47.482 --> 00:13:49.450
Let's hope.


00:13:49.484 --> 00:13:51.315
So...


00:13:53.655 --> 00:13:55.623
What the hell?


00:13:55.657 --> 00:13:56.783
Life is worth living.


00:13:56.825 --> 00:13:59.316
Isn't it?


00:14:10.072 --> 00:14:14.805
- The death rate
just kept on climbing.


00:14:14.843 --> 00:14:16.140
We realized that science


00:14:16.178 --> 00:14:19.238
really was up against
a brick wall.


00:14:19.281 --> 00:14:21.146
We kept getting new drugs
approved


00:14:21.183 --> 00:14:22.810
to prevent
opportunistic infections,


00:14:22.851 --> 00:14:25.513
and then somebody would just
get another infection.


00:15:00.389 --> 00:15:02.050
- So, Peter,
where are we going?


00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:03.853
- We're gonna be going
to the headquarters


00:15:03.892 --> 00:15:08.022
of Daiichi pharmaceutical
companies of Japan.


00:15:08.063 --> 00:15:10.224
This is
their U.S. headquarters,


00:15:10.265 --> 00:15:12.859
and we're blockading
their offices


00:15:12.901 --> 00:15:15.028
because they have a drug


00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:17.368
that's important
both to AIDS activists


00:15:17.406 --> 00:15:19.533
and to cancer activists,


00:15:19.574 --> 00:15:23.374
specifically
breast cancer,


00:15:23.412 --> 00:15:27.041
that they've been
dragging their feet on


00:15:27.082 --> 00:15:28.879
for over two years now,


00:15:28.917 --> 00:15:31.215
and we don't understand why,


00:15:31.253 --> 00:15:35.053
but we certainly are gonna
try to let them understand


00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:37.115
why we're concerned.


00:15:37.159 --> 00:15:38.148
And, everybody...


00:15:38.193 --> 00:15:39.717
- Wait for you
at the end of the hall.


00:15:39.761 --> 00:15:42.229
- Just wait
outside the elevators.


00:15:42.264 --> 00:15:44.732
- Shh.


00:15:44.766 --> 00:15:45.892
- Hey.


00:15:45.934 --> 00:15:47.401
Hi, we're with ACT UP.


00:15:47.436 --> 00:15:49.404
We're doing
an act of civil disobedience.


00:15:49.438 --> 00:15:52.236
Please remain calm.


00:15:52.274 --> 00:15:54.242
Jim, it's Peter.
We're in.


00:15:54.276 --> 00:15:56.540
Send all the press.


00:15:56.578 --> 00:15:59.445
- Hello,
we're from ACT UP New York.


00:16:07.856 --> 00:16:09.084
- You already have the blood


00:16:09.124 --> 00:16:11.183
of several thousand people
on your hands,


00:16:11.226 --> 00:16:12.420
and those of us like me


00:16:12.461 --> 00:16:15.089
who have Kaposi's sarcoma
are gonna die,


00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:17.564
and we are here
until we get arrested.


00:16:17.599 --> 00:16:19.760
- You seem to know nothing
about the actual details


00:16:19.801 --> 00:16:21.428
of the development
of this drug.


00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:23.131
Maybe you're just
not telling us.


00:16:23.171 --> 00:16:26.038
- Mr. Borsic, have you scheduled
a meeting with the FDA?


00:16:26.074 --> 00:16:27.336
- Yeah, as soon as we can.


00:16:27.375 --> 00:16:29.775
- We have helped many companies
through this process.


00:16:29.811 --> 00:16:33.269
We can take a drug from
your test tube to the market


00:16:33.315 --> 00:16:35.613
in under two years
if you work with us,


00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.447
and we will pave the way
for you


00:16:37.486 --> 00:16:39.283
with the Food and Drug
Administration.


00:16:39.321 --> 00:16:41.789
But this total reluctance
on your part


00:16:41.823 --> 00:16:43.017
is gonna get you nowhere.


00:16:43.058 --> 00:16:44.958
- Have been used in people
for 30 years.


00:16:44.993 --> 00:16:47.052
- It'll end up killing us,
all right?


00:16:47.095 --> 00:16:48.960
- See this dark mark
on my forehead?


00:16:48.997 --> 00:16:51.295
That's Kaposi's sarcoma.


00:16:51.333 --> 00:16:52.800
It's gonna spread!


00:16:52.834 --> 00:16:54.131
It's gonna kill me.


00:16:54.169 --> 00:16:55.796
You coming to my funeral?


00:16:55.837 --> 00:16:58.305
Because you're the man
fucking responsible.


00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:01.673
You are my murderer
in your shirt and tie.


00:17:06.014 --> 00:17:09.142
- Do you think
that you'll live to see a cure?


00:17:09.184 --> 00:17:10.310
- No.


00:17:10.352 --> 00:17:11.785
I don't.


00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:15.654
- Do you think
that you'll live?


00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:18.557
- No. No.


00:17:18.593 --> 00:17:21.721
- You expect to die from this?


00:17:36.378 --> 00:17:38.676
- The anger just mounted
and mounted and mounted


00:17:38.713 --> 00:17:40.681
the more people
who were dying.


00:17:40.715 --> 00:17:43.513
Once a week, we met.


00:17:43.552 --> 00:17:44.712
And at that meeting,


00:17:44.753 --> 00:17:46.846
a lot of people came
who were just terrified


00:17:46.888 --> 00:17:50.016
they weren't gonna be alive
even the next week.


00:17:50.058 --> 00:17:52.492
What can we do?
How can we get there?


00:17:52.527 --> 00:17:55.985
- I think ACT UP's anger
turned in


00:17:56.031 --> 00:17:59.865
after having been directed out
so long.


00:17:59.901 --> 00:18:02.233
In its first few years,


00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:05.706
Treatment and Data pretty much
got everything it wanted


00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.208
from the floor of ACT UP,


00:18:08.243 --> 00:18:11.371
but as Treatment and Data
was becoming


00:18:11.413 --> 00:18:13.381
more and more technical,


00:18:13.415 --> 00:18:17.715
there were a lot of people in
the general membership of ACT UP


00:18:17.752 --> 00:18:20.550
that saw that as an elite,


00:18:20.589 --> 00:18:22.386
and that maybe
it would be better


00:18:22.424 --> 00:18:27.521
if that elite
was pulled in a bit.


00:18:27.562 --> 00:18:29.223
- There was a fear, I think,


00:18:29.264 --> 00:18:33.667
that we were getting too close
to the people in power,


00:18:33.702 --> 00:18:36.136
that we would compromise
our own principles.


00:18:36.171 --> 00:18:41.074
And the people who were more
interested in the social issues


00:18:41.109 --> 00:18:42.701
became uncomfortable
with that.


00:18:42.744 --> 00:18:44.234
- I remember
this very divisive moment


00:18:44.279 --> 00:18:46.076
where, um, you know,


00:18:46.114 --> 00:18:48.241
there was a proposal
for moratorium


00:18:48.283 --> 00:18:51.741
on meeting with drug companies,
and someone--


00:18:51.786 --> 00:18:53.083
for six months--


00:18:53.121 --> 00:18:55.749
and there was a huge
and impassioned debate over it,


00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:56.916
and someone said--


00:18:56.958 --> 00:18:59.756
a woman who was not
HIV-positive said,


00:18:59.794 --> 00:19:02.092
"Well, it's not like
it's for the rest of your life."


00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:05.099
And for a lot of people
in the room,


00:19:05.133 --> 00:19:06.896
it was the rest of their life.


00:19:06.935 --> 00:19:08.926
Act up!
Fight back!


00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:10.096
Fight AIDS!


00:19:10.138 --> 00:19:13.596
- There were inevitable
splits in priorities.


00:19:13.642 --> 00:19:15.473
- You know it quite well.
- I know.


00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.102
- And it was completely
left out


00:19:17.145 --> 00:19:19.272
of the NIH research agenda.


00:19:19.314 --> 00:19:21.612
- I agree.
I--I--


00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:24.278
- I remember a lot of
dirty tricks that happened


00:19:24.319 --> 00:19:28.449
and a lot of fear
within the organization


00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:31.459
that the various factions
had done this to each other.


00:19:31.493 --> 00:19:33.120
- Mark Harrington,


00:19:33.161 --> 00:19:34.458
Mark Harrington,


00:19:34.496 --> 00:19:36.794
there's a video camera
here now.


00:19:36.831 --> 00:19:38.458
Would you like
to take an oath


00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.663
that you will not write nasty
anonymous letters to people?


00:19:41.703 --> 00:19:43.466
- I've been getting
some hate letters too,


00:19:43.505 --> 00:19:44.631
but those are unsigned.


00:19:44.673 --> 00:19:46.140
I don't ever--
I don't ever--


00:19:46.174 --> 00:19:48.802
- So you'll keep on
writing nasty letters to people?


00:19:48.843 --> 00:19:51.141
- There were a lot of charges


00:19:51.179 --> 00:19:54.273
in the midst of that,
of sabotage and threats.


00:19:54.315 --> 00:19:58.445
- Our last speaker is--
is Larry Kramer.


00:19:58.486 --> 00:20:00.647
- Why didn't you
answer the charges?


00:20:00.689 --> 00:20:02.816
- Bill, you're gonna
have a chance to talk.


00:20:02.857 --> 00:20:04.017
All right, everybody's--


00:20:04.059 --> 00:20:05.151
- Don't lecture me,


00:20:05.193 --> 00:20:07.661
you stupid, lazy,
incompetent shithead!


00:20:07.696 --> 00:20:10.062
- Bill,
everybody got the flyer--


00:20:11.866 --> 00:20:14.460
- You can't just lick his ass
before he talks!


00:20:14.502 --> 00:20:16.834
- Shut the fuck up
and let him answer!


00:20:16.871 --> 00:20:18.998
- Look, there are a lot of
people in the audience


00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:21.338
who want to ask
and talk about treatment,


00:20:21.376 --> 00:20:24.345
and I think it's important
that we allow that to happen.


00:20:24.379 --> 00:20:26.244
- Oh, we're gonna dictate
free speech now?


00:20:26.281 --> 00:20:27.714
- You're the one
who's interfering


00:20:27.749 --> 00:20:28.875
with speech right now.


00:20:28.917 --> 00:20:30.384
- Go back to GMHC


00:20:30.418 --> 00:20:32.682
or whatever AIDS pimp operation
is paying you.


00:20:32.721 --> 00:20:34.689
You're making the same point
George Bush made--


00:20:34.723 --> 00:20:36.350
- Plague!


00:20:36.391 --> 00:20:39.189
We are in the middle
of a fucking plague!


00:20:39.227 --> 00:20:41.559
And you behave like this!


00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:51.164
Plague!


00:20:51.206 --> 00:20:56.075
40 million infected people
is a fucking plague!


00:21:01.583 --> 00:21:03.710
We are in the worst shape


00:21:03.752 --> 00:21:08.382
we have ever, ever,
ever been in!


00:21:08.423 --> 00:21:11.051
All those pills we're shoveling
down our throats,


00:21:11.092 --> 00:21:13.219
forget it!


00:21:13.261 --> 00:21:16.389
ACT UP has been taken over
by a lunatic fringe.


00:21:16.431 --> 00:21:17.591
They can't get together.


00:21:17.632 --> 00:21:18.860
Nobody agrees with anything.


00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:20.231
All we can do


00:21:20.268 --> 00:21:23.396
is field a couple hundred people
in a demonstration!


00:21:23.438 --> 00:21:28.068
That's not gonna make anybody
pay attention!


00:21:28.109 --> 00:21:31.738
Not until we get millions
out there!


00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:33.407
And we can't do that!


00:21:33.448 --> 00:21:35.416
All we do
is pick at each other


00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:37.543
and yell at each other!


00:21:37.585 --> 00:21:40.179
And I say to you
in year ten


00:21:40.221 --> 00:21:44.419
the same thing
I said to you in 1981


00:21:44.459 --> 00:21:48.759
when there were 41 cases.


00:21:48.797 --> 00:21:50.924
Until we get our acts
together,


00:21:50.965 --> 00:21:54.594
all of us,


00:21:54.636 --> 00:21:57.469
we are as good as dead.


00:22:01.309 --> 00:22:02.936
- In the end,
the Treatment and Data guys--


00:22:02.977 --> 00:22:06.276
Peter, Garance, Mark,
and some others--


00:22:06.314 --> 00:22:10.614
split off and formed
their own separate organization.


00:22:10.652 --> 00:22:12.620
- TAG was one of the little
mercury balls


00:22:12.654 --> 00:22:15.282
that flew off the main body
of ACT UP.


00:22:15.323 --> 00:22:19.657
A more sort of "think tank"
type project came about.


00:22:21.162 --> 00:22:23.130
- Mr. Harrington,
a TAG member,


00:22:23.164 --> 00:22:24.961
educated at Harvard College,


00:22:24.999 --> 00:22:27.126
and he has worked
for a long time


00:22:27.168 --> 00:22:30.137
on experimental treatments
for the disease


00:22:30.171 --> 00:22:32.139
and also the basic science.


00:22:32.173 --> 00:22:36.303
And Mr. Gonsalves
was born in Long Island


00:22:36.344 --> 00:22:39.404
and attended Tufts University,
also a TAG member.


00:22:39.447 --> 00:22:41.972
I guess
I can do nothing better


00:22:42.016 --> 00:22:45.315
than to turn this conference
over to my speakers.


00:22:46.521 --> 00:22:47.818
- I noticed that you're both


00:22:47.856 --> 00:22:51.485
sitting up there
in suits and ties.


00:22:51.526 --> 00:22:53.994
Do you feel that
your approach


00:22:54.028 --> 00:22:58.658
is better than circling
NIH buildings


00:22:58.700 --> 00:23:00.167
and so forth?


00:23:00.201 --> 00:23:03.170
- I think that we
like to keep our options open,


00:23:03.204 --> 00:23:06.571
but it's silly to risk arrest


00:23:06.608 --> 00:23:08.235
and the hassles
that are attendant upon it


00:23:08.276 --> 00:23:11.336
if you can get serious attention
and negotiations going


00:23:11.379 --> 00:23:13.847
with other measures.


00:23:13.882 --> 00:23:15.509
- We've just released
a report,


00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:17.882
a critique of
all the NIH's AIDS programs.


00:23:17.919 --> 00:23:20.183
- The research is spread out
over 12 agencies.


00:23:20.221 --> 00:23:21.347
There's no coordination.


00:23:21.389 --> 00:23:23.186
There's a lot of duplication.


00:23:23.224 --> 00:23:24.691
There's no leadership.


00:23:24.726 --> 00:23:27.354
- The budget is shrinking
and shrinking as cases mount,


00:23:27.395 --> 00:23:29.022
and the president
needs to be blamed,


00:23:29.063 --> 00:23:30.428
as well as the Congress,


00:23:30.465 --> 00:23:32.194
who cut the entire NIH budget


00:23:32.233 --> 00:23:34.098
by $150 million
two weeks ago.


00:23:34.135 --> 00:23:35.534
- Our recommendations,
I think,


00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:37.538
are gonna require
some legislation.


00:23:37.572 --> 00:23:41.201
So we have to go
to our friends on the hill


00:23:41.242 --> 00:23:43.733
and see what wonders
they can work for us.


00:23:54.422 --> 00:23:56.390
- We had
this one particular compound


00:23:56.424 --> 00:23:59.222
that looked like
it may have had the potency


00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:01.888
and the physical properties
that we wanted,


00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:03.864
and it could be
a possible drug.


00:24:03.898 --> 00:24:05.365
- We said, you know,
"Let's put this


00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:07.800
in HIV-infected individuals,
and let's see what happens."


00:24:07.835 --> 00:24:10.235
So we went into
HIV-infected individuals


00:24:10.271 --> 00:24:11.898
with this drug
called Crixivan,


00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:14.101
and you could see
a very substantial drop


00:24:14.142 --> 00:24:15.769
just with
the one protease inhibitor;


00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:18.005
you could see a very substantial
drop in virus load.


00:24:18.046 --> 00:24:19.343
So that was the first week.


00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:21.075
The second week
was very disappointing,


00:24:21.115 --> 00:24:24.107
because what we saw
in the second week was, in fact,


00:24:24.152 --> 00:24:26.916
the virus load
coming right back up again.


00:24:26.955 --> 00:24:28.115
One exception.


00:24:28.156 --> 00:24:30.090
- There was one patient that--


00:24:30.124 --> 00:24:34.754
patient 143, I believe,
was his name--his number--


00:24:34.796 --> 00:24:37.492
that the virus went down
and stayed down.


00:24:37.532 --> 00:24:40.092
- That told us
that it was possible.


00:24:40.134 --> 00:24:41.601
If it can happen in one,


00:24:41.636 --> 00:24:44.434
then by definition
it can happen in everyone.


00:24:44.472 --> 00:24:46.337
You just need to figure out
how to do it.


00:24:46.374 --> 00:24:48.604
That puts you
in a completely different place


00:24:48.643 --> 00:24:50.770
and in a completely different
state of mind.


00:24:50.812 --> 00:24:52.109
So then the question became,


00:24:52.146 --> 00:24:53.613
"Okay, now what do
we need to do


00:24:53.648 --> 00:24:55.912
in order to make it
possible?"


00:24:58.152 --> 00:25:00.620
- This is the beginning
of the primary season


00:25:00.655 --> 00:25:02.520
to elect the next president.


00:25:02.557 --> 00:25:05.617
We want to send a message
to all of the candidates:


00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:10.757
we have not seen them actively
address the AIDS plague,


00:25:10.798 --> 00:25:13.289
and we thought it would be best
to send a message


00:25:13.334 --> 00:25:15.962
by voting with our feet
in the streets.


00:25:16.004 --> 00:25:20.703
I want to call for
a massive march on Washington.


00:25:20.742 --> 00:25:24.473
The weekend the AIDS quilt
is gonna be there,


00:25:24.512 --> 00:25:27.310
we have got to
surround the White House


00:25:27.348 --> 00:25:30.215
with people
concerned about AIDS


00:25:30.251 --> 00:25:33.482
to push Bush
out of the White House!


00:25:38.860 --> 00:25:41.658
- Last night, a man with AIDS
heckled Clinton,


00:25:41.696 --> 00:25:43.493
charging that
he had a bad record


00:25:43.531 --> 00:25:45.829
on fighting AIDS
in Arkansas.


00:25:45.867 --> 00:25:47.994
- When voter Bob Rafsky
met Bill Clinton,


00:25:48.036 --> 00:25:49.663
it was anything
but pleasant.


00:25:49.704 --> 00:25:51.501
- We're dying in this state!


00:25:51.539 --> 00:25:54.667
What are you going to do
about AIDS?


00:25:54.709 --> 00:25:57.337
- First of all,
it will become


00:25:57.378 --> 00:25:59.938
a part of my obsession
as president.


00:26:02.517 --> 00:26:04.178
- That's why
I'm running for president,


00:26:04.218 --> 00:26:05.685
to do something about it.


00:26:05.720 --> 00:26:07.017
- Now, will you just calm down?


00:26:09.390 --> 00:26:12.018
I feel your pain!


00:26:12.060 --> 00:26:13.357
I feel your pain.


00:26:13.394 --> 00:26:15.021
But if you want to attack me
personally,


00:26:15.063 --> 00:26:16.462
you're no better
than Jerry Brown


00:26:16.497 --> 00:26:17.725
and all the rest
of these people


00:26:17.765 --> 00:26:19.528
who say whatever sounds good
in the moment.


00:26:19.567 --> 00:26:20.829
If you want something
to be done,


00:26:20.868 --> 00:26:22.529
you ask me a question,
and you listen.


00:26:22.570 --> 00:26:23.696
If you don't agree with me,


00:26:23.738 --> 00:26:25.535
go support somebody else
for president,


00:26:25.573 --> 00:26:27.040
but quit talking to me
like that.


00:26:27.075 --> 00:26:28.872
This is not a matter
of personal attack;


00:26:28.910 --> 00:26:30.707
it's a matter of human loss.


00:26:33.081 --> 00:26:36.050
- I came here tonight
because I'm dying from AIDS.


00:26:36.084 --> 00:26:38.712
And it doesn't matter to me
who the next president is


00:26:38.753 --> 00:26:41.881
if they don't change
11 years of government neglect


00:26:41.923 --> 00:26:43.550
of this epidemic.


00:26:43.591 --> 00:26:45.388
- Is this on?
This isn't on.


00:26:45.426 --> 00:26:48.827
Um, okay, first off,


00:26:48.863 --> 00:26:51.730
what happened this week was,


00:26:51.766 --> 00:26:55.793
AIDS became an issue
in this campaign.


00:27:02.276 --> 00:27:04.744
I'd like to call down
Bob Rafsky.


00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:27.097
- Act up!


00:27:27.135 --> 00:27:28.432
Fight back!


00:27:28.469 --> 00:27:29.697
Fight AIDS!


00:27:29.737 --> 00:27:31.864
Act up!
Fight back!


00:27:31.906 --> 00:27:33.066
Fight AIDS!


00:27:37.378 --> 00:27:38.936
- Uh, never debate
a Rhodes scholar.


00:27:38.980 --> 00:27:41.005
It gets you
into a world of trouble.


00:27:42.183 --> 00:27:43.878
It looks like
what we have to do


00:27:43.918 --> 00:27:47.285
is to keep forcing these clowns
to say the right thing


00:27:47.321 --> 00:27:49.448
so that if one of them happens
to become president,


00:27:49.490 --> 00:27:51.924
we can hold them accountable
for doing the right thing.


00:27:51.959 --> 00:27:53.187
- Yeah.


00:27:53.227 --> 00:27:55.457
- But I just--
it's always important to say


00:27:55.496 --> 00:27:57.123
that we all know that


00:27:57.165 --> 00:27:59.793
the names of the people
who might save our lives


00:27:59.834 --> 00:28:02.462
are not Bill Clinton
and Jerry Brown, et cetera.


00:28:02.503 --> 00:28:04.971
The names of the people
who might save our lives


00:28:05.006 --> 00:28:06.803
are Iris Long,
Mark Harrington,


00:28:06.841 --> 00:28:08.468
Peter Staley, et cetera.


00:28:08.509 --> 00:28:10.477
And they're the ones
who will be remembered


00:28:10.511 --> 00:28:12.308
as the heroes
of this epidemic,


00:28:12.346 --> 00:28:14.974
as well as those
who have gone before.


00:28:18.586 --> 00:28:20.213
- ♪ And he smells like one too ♪


00:28:20.254 --> 00:28:21.448
- Well, I haven't showered,


00:28:21.489 --> 00:28:23.480
so I'm not surprised
that you would say that.


00:28:23.524 --> 00:28:26.152
No, I've just been writing,
and...


00:28:26.194 --> 00:28:28.162
I was up at 5:00 a.m.
yesterday.


00:28:28.196 --> 00:28:30.824
- This is Bob's birthday,


00:28:30.865 --> 00:28:34.426
July 22, 1992.


00:28:34.468 --> 00:28:35.662
- Ready for the pyrotechnics?


00:28:35.703 --> 00:28:36.727
- Yes!


00:28:36.771 --> 00:28:37.760
- Nathaniel, help.


00:28:37.805 --> 00:28:39.830
- No!


00:28:39.874 --> 00:28:42.172
- Yay!


00:28:42.210 --> 00:28:45.839
- Lydia E. Rios.


00:28:45.880 --> 00:28:49.338
Steve H.


00:28:49.383 --> 00:28:53.342
My friends, David Evans,


00:28:53.387 --> 00:28:58.689
Nicolas Kaiser,
George Marshall,


00:28:58.726 --> 00:29:02.924
and my beloved brother
Dennis J.


00:29:02.964 --> 00:29:06.456
- Robert R. Hakins.


00:29:06.500 --> 00:29:10.527
Phillip Gregory Ellison.


00:29:10.571 --> 00:29:13.369
Terry Ronan.


00:29:13.407 --> 00:29:16.274
- Michael Bennett.


00:29:16.310 --> 00:29:18.369
Ron Field.


00:29:18.412 --> 00:29:20.880
Tina Chow.


00:29:20.915 --> 00:29:23.281
Perry Ellis.


00:29:23.317 --> 00:29:25.376
Freddie Mercury.


00:29:25.419 --> 00:29:28.047
Peter Allen.


00:29:28.089 --> 00:29:30.887
To the thousands
of other people


00:29:30.925 --> 00:29:34.417
who were made to suffer
in silence.


00:29:40.768 --> 00:29:44.397
- Join ACT UP
for a political funeral!


00:29:44.438 --> 00:29:47.737
Meet at the steps of the Capitol
at 1:00 p.m.


00:29:47.775 --> 00:29:49.072
Give a wake-up call


00:29:49.110 --> 00:29:52.568
to George Bush and Bill Clinton
and Perot.


00:29:59.287 --> 00:30:02.051
- I think the quilt itself
does good stuff


00:30:02.089 --> 00:30:03.454
and is moving.


00:30:03.491 --> 00:30:05.425
Still, it's like
making something beautiful


00:30:05.459 --> 00:30:07.324
out of the epidemic.


00:30:07.361 --> 00:30:09.192
And I felt like
doing something like this


00:30:09.230 --> 00:30:10.390
is a way of showing


00:30:10.431 --> 00:30:11.864
there's nothing beautiful
about it.


00:30:11.899 --> 00:30:13.298
You know,
this is what I'm left with.


00:30:13.334 --> 00:30:15.268
I've got a box full of ashes
and bone chips.


00:30:15.303 --> 00:30:17.430
You know,
there's no beauty in that.


00:30:17.471 --> 00:30:20.599
And I felt like a statement
like this is like saying,


00:30:20.641 --> 00:30:22.609
"This is what George Bush
has done," you know?


00:30:22.643 --> 00:30:23.769
This is what him


00:30:23.811 --> 00:30:25.335
and Ronald Reagan before him
have done.


00:30:25.379 --> 00:30:26.573
These are our loved ones,


00:30:26.614 --> 00:30:28.013
and this is what they've been
reduced to,


00:30:28.049 --> 00:30:29.209
and we're bringing them


00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:31.150
to the person who's responsible
for their death.


